            <ArticleTitle>Results of insemination (AIH) following GnRH treatment of endometriosis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>243-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Endometriosis is one of the most frequent benign diseases in gynecology. It is the cause of the pelvic pain and infertility in more than 35% of women of reproductive age. The most appropriate treatment for endometriosis is the combination of surgery and adjuvant medical therapy with GnRH agonists. The authors demonstrate the results of 33 artificial intrauterine homolog inseminations after a 6-month GnRH analog therapy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
